<p>Two new door styles just joined the narrow-rail lineup for both <a href="/brands/shiloh-cabinetry/">Shiloh Cabinetry</a> and <a href="/brands/eclipse-cabinetry/">Eclipse Cabinetry</a>: <strong>Pacifica</strong> and <strong>Ventura</strong>. Both are flat-panel doors framed by a slim <strong>5/16" applied moulding</strong> — about a third the width of a traditional slim shaker rail. The difference between them is the profile of that moulding: Pacifica's is <strong>radiused</strong>, Ventura's is <strong>square</strong>. That one detail decides whether the door reads soft and transitional or crisp and modern.</p>

<p>Because both styles are offered on Shiloh and Eclipse, you can put the same door on a face-frame Shiloh kitchen or a frameless Eclipse kitchen. Pick the construction for the project, then pick the door. Not sure which construction fits? See <a href="/playbook/frameless-vs-face-frame-cabinets/">Frameless vs. Face-Frame Cabinets</a>.</p>

